1
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:38,500
A missing father. A desperate search. An unforgettable adventure.

2
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Alaska is a family, drama, adventure film directed by Fraser Clarke Heston.

3
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:43,500
Jake Barnes and his two kids, Sean and Jessie, have
moved to Alaska after his wife died.

4
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:16,000
He is a former airline pilot now delivering toilet paper across the mountains.

5
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:48,500
During an emergency delivery in a storm his plane
goes down somewhere in the mountains.

6
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:21,000
Annoyed that the authorities aren't doing enough, Jessie and Sean set out on an adventure to find their
father with the help of a polar bear which they have saved from a ferocious poacher.

7
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:53,500
Conflict ensues.

8
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:26,000
Jessie Barnes, played by Thora Birch.

9
00:40:52,500 --> 00:40:58,500
Sean Barnes, played by Vincent Kartheiser.

10
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:31,000
Jake Barnes, played by Dirk Benedict.

11
00:49:57,500 --> 00:50:03,500
Charlie, Quincy Air Service, played by Ben Cardinal.

12
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Florence, played by Kristin Lehman.

13
00:59:02,500 --> 00:59:08,500
Trooper Sam Harvey, played by Stephen E. Miller.

14
01:03:35,000 --> 01:03:41,000
Alaska is a 1996 American adventure survival film directed by Fraser
Clarke Heston and produced by Carol Fuchs and Andy Burg.

15
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:13,500
The story, written by Burg and Scott Myers, centers on two children who
search through the Alaskan wilderness for their lost father.

16
01:12:40,000 --> 01:12:46,000
During their journey, they find a polar bear who
helps lead them to their father.

17
01:17:12,500 --> 01:17:18,500
However, a poacher with a desire to capture the bear follows
close behind the children and the polar bear.

18
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:51,000
The director's father, Charlton Heston, plays the main antagonist.

19
01:26:17,500 --> 01:26:23,500
The movie was filmed primarily in the Purcell Mountains of
British Columbia in Canada and the city of Vancouver.

20
01:30:50,000 --> 01:30:56,000
The film was a box office bomb, grossing only
$11,829,959 against a $24 million budget.

21
01:35:22,500 --> 01:35:28,500
It received negative reviews upon its release.

22
01:39:55,000 --> 01:40:01,000
The film explores themes of pilot, polar bear, poacher, alaska, airplane crash.

23
01:44:27,500 --> 01:44:33,500
The tone is emotional.
